1
00:00:01,190 --> 00:00:07,940
A Place of Our Own

2
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:09,630
How do you do?

3
00:00:09,630 --> 00:00:11,360
Hello.

4
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:12,430
I'm Ralph Riley.

5
00:00:12,430 --> 00:00:15,040
I'm Richard Stewart, and this is my wife, Marilyn.

6
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:15,680
Pleased to meet you.

7
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:16,480
Likewise, Mr. Riley.

8
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:21,220
Please, sit down. What can I do for you?

9
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:24,000
We'd like to discuss a mortgage.

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,930
For a house.

11
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:27,300
Fine. Are you buying a house

12
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,200
or are you refinancing your present home?

13
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:31,080
We're planning to buy a house.

14
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:33,400
And we'd like to find out about a mortgage.

15
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:35,340
We are customers of the bank.

16
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:38,310
As a matter of fact, my whole family banks here.

17
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:41,670
I have some questions to ask.

18
00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:44,170
Do you own your house or do you rent?

19
00:00:44,170 --> 00:00:45,120
Neither.

20
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:50,180
We live with my parents, Dr. and Mrs. Philip Stewart.

21
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:52,180
And how old are you?

22
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:53,160
I'm twenty-nine.

23
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:55,630
I'm thirty.

24
00:00:55,630 --> 00:00:58,440
And, Mr. Stewart, what is your occupation?

25
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:00,300
I'm a freelance photographer.

26
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,830
And, Mrs. Stewart, are you working?

27
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:05,300
Yes. I'm a designer, and I work in a boutique.

28
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:07,880
Did you bring any savings or salary information?

29
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:09,130
Last year's tax forms?

30
00:01:09,130 --> 00:01:17,210
Yes. Here they are.

31
00:01:17,210 --> 00:01:19,900
OK. What ... what kind of house did you have in mind?

32
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:21,020
We're talking about buying

33
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:23,300
a two-bedroom house in Mount Kisco.

34
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:29,410
Here are the financial details on the house.

35
00:01:29,410 --> 00:01:30,340
Thank you.

36
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:31,850
Are you prepared to make a ten-percent down payment?

37
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:33,620
Yes, we are.

38
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:35,440
Payments over thirty years?

39
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:39,300
Yes.

40
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:41,730
Do you think we can get a loan?

41
00:01:41,730 --> 00:01:46,270
Well, it depends. Do you own any other property?

42
00:01:46,270 --> 00:01:49,380
Any stocks or bonds?

43
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:51,480
No.

44
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:56,140
I see. Then you don't have any collateral.

45
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:58,460
Perhaps you could get a guarantor--

46
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:01,100
someone to sign for the loan for you.

47
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:03,160
Why is that necessary?

48
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,510
Since you don't have enough income,

49
00:02:04,510 --> 00:02:06,620
and you don't already own any property,

50
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:07,950
the bank needs to be sure

51
00:02:07,950 --> 00:02:09,850
you can pay the mortgage every month.

52
00:02:09,850 --> 00:02:11,840
A guarantor is responsible for the loan

53
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:14,140
if you can't make the payments.

54
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:21,010
I see. Well, the idea of buying a house is exciting.

55
00:02:21,010 --> 00:02:24,800
Thank you, Mr. Riley. We'll read this over carefully.

56
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:25,860
Thank you.

57
00:02:25,860 --> 00:02:26,930
Good-bye. Thanks.

58
00:02:26,930 --> 00:02:30,540
Good-bye. And hope to see you soon.

59
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:31,210
I hope so, too.

60
00:02:31,210 --> 00:02:32,470
Take care.

61
00:02:32,470 --> 00:02:52,470
Good-bye.

62
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:53,370
It all sounded so easy

63
00:02:53,370 --> 00:02:57,600
until they mentioned needing collateral or a guarantor.

64
00:02:57,600 --> 00:03:00,620
We have no collateral.

65
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:01,980
And I don't think it's a good idea

66
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:05,180
to ask Dad to sign as a guarantor.

67
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:06,750
I don't feel right about it.

68
00:03:06,750 --> 00:03:22,090
I understand your feelings about it, Richard.

69
00:03:22,090 --> 00:03:29,990
We can get a loan from the bank

70
00:03:29,990 --> 00:03:31,340
[03:25.43]if we can put up some collateral.

71
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:33,580
And we don't own anything to use as collateral.

72
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:39,200
Or someone can sign with us as a guarantor.

73
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,110
Why don't you speak to Dad?

74
00:03:41,110 --> 00:03:46,260
No. If we buy a house, I want to be able to handle it alone.

75
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:49,450
Everybody needs help sometimes, Richard.

76
00:03:49,450 --> 00:03:51,620
I understand Richard's feelings about it, Ellen.

77
00:03:51,620 --> 00:03:54,460
In two or three months, I'll have an advance on my book

78
00:03:54,460 --> 00:03:57,500
and be able to put more money down.

79
00:03:57,500 --> 00:04:00,790
What about the house in Mount Kisco?

80
00:04:00,790 --> 00:04:02,850
Somebody else'll buy it by then.

81
00:04:02,850 --> 00:04:05,720
Then there'll be other houses, Marilyn.

82
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:10,320
Richard has a point. You're just beginning to look. Richard

83
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:11,380
We're in no great rush. It's true.

84
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:13,560
This has been a great learning experience for us, Marilyn.

85
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,650
Talking to the real-estate agent.

86
00:04:15,650 --> 00:04:18,000
Looking at the houses.

87
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,820
Talking to the loan officer at the bank.

88
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:23,950
It has been a learning experience. That's true.

89
00:04:23,950 --> 00:04:26,670
I think you're doing the right thing. Taking your time.

90
00:04:26,670 --> 00:04:30,110
Looking around. Especially with a purchase of this kind.

91
00:04:30,110 --> 00:04:33,670
You're talking about a lot of money.

92
00:04:33,670 --> 00:04:37,140
We'll call Mrs. Martinelli and tell her to keep looking for us.

93
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:42,130
And I'll call Mr. Riley at the bank

94
00:04:42,130 --> 00:04:42,810
and tell him we'll see him in a couple of months.

95
00:04:42,810 --> 00:04:45,150
And if you ever need Dad or me to help you ...

96
00:04:45,150 --> 00:04:46,230
We know.

97
00:04:46,230 --> 00:04:48,410
You know we'll be there for you.

98
00:04:48,410 --> 00:04:51,410
It's a Stewart tradition. We're a family.
